{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ישכן לבטח", :translit "yishkon lavetach", :gloss "he shall dwell securely"} {:he "ולערב יחלק שלל", :translit "u'la'arev yechalek shalal", :gloss "and at evening he shall divide the spoil"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Links the wolf imagery of Benjamin's tribal identity across Genesis and Deuteronomy blessings."}], :frame {:text "Jacob blessed Benjamin with the words 'בנימין זאב יטרף ולערב יחלק שלל' (Genesis 49:27). Moses' blessing that Benjamin 'shall dwell securely' is read as the aftermath of the wolf's success — dividing spoil at evening is the state of tranquility. Ba'al HaTurim reads Moses' blessing as the sequel to Jacob's.", :sources ["Genesis 49:27" "Deuteronomy 33:12"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ובין כתיפיו", :translit "u'vein katfeiv", :gloss "and between his shoulders"} {:he "ובירושלם", :translit "u'vi'yerushalayim", :gloss "and in Jerusalem"} {:he "ובין כתפיו שכן", :translit "u'vein katfeiv shachan", :gloss "and between his shoulders He dwelt"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ובין כתיפיו", :b "ובירושלם"}], :frame {:text "Moses' blessing over Benjamin states 'ובין כתפיו שכן' (Deuteronomy 33:12), understood to mean that God dwells between Benjamin's shoulders — i.e., the Temple in Jerusalem is located in Benjamin's tribal portion. The equation of ובין כתיפיו with ובירושלם confirms this geographic identification.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 33:12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Links the wolf imagery of Benjamin's tribal identity across Genesis and Deuteronomy blessings.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "ובין כתיפיו", :a-value 594, :b "ובירושלם", :b-value 594, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:41:22.314192871Z", :model "glm-5.2"}